{
  "comment": [
    "A Guardian Rises (act_cosmo_m0_highway): the start of the first mission, as a stand-in activity-host script.",
    "Use with bap_server.py --ah-mission missions/a_guardian_rises.json (see notes/mission-director.md).",
    "Order from the reference recording: revival cinematic (third person, then first person), 'Enter the Wall',",
    "trigger at the Wall, 'Find a Weapon' in The Breach, the Ghost's light (pf_104a_pwr), 'Grab the Rifle'.",
    "Field meanings are from the EBOOT handlers; the values marked in the note as guesses are what the runs test.",
    "Triggers (kind 0x1d): +0 true arms the trigger; the client reports once per arming, when its last report is older than",
    "the arming time at +4 (0xb2fb68), so +4 = \"$now\" and --ah-sim-clock is required. Which client message carries the",
    "report is not known yet, so the trigger steps match the trigger's object id in any client message type.",
    "Objectives: 1 = active; 3 = complete (the handler special-cases 3, and the state-3 case of 0x355abc calls into the",
    "character/progress code); 2 looks like 'active with progress counters'. Squads (kind 1): a new +0x44 generation re-runs",
    "the squad; squad_existing_members means +0x5c on 01.00 or +0x74 on 01.24 (0 destroy, 1 release, -1 nothing).",
    "spawn members is still unknown; the Breach squads are placed 20 s after the client reports slice set 24.",
    "Objective states (01.24, JOIN60): 1 = incoming (the 'NEW MISSION' banner with the activity name, about 4 s), 5 = active:",
    "the title (and on change its description) shows at the left of the HUD. Each objective is set to 1 and 6 s later to 5.",
    "3 is still used for completion (special-cased by the handler); its on-screen effect is not confirmed yet.",
    "Handover (JOIN70): the completed objective goes to 3 (with its completion sequence), 4 s later to 0 while the next",
    "objective starts (1, incoming sequence step 1, trigger armed), and 6 s after that the next objective goes to 5."
  ],
